      },
      "note": "Reviewed 2026-09-01 at this revision. Build-tool plugin attached unconditionally to mlx-swift's core Cmlx target, so it cannot be taken out of the graph without forking mlx-swift. Read in full (Plugins/CudaBuild/plugin.swift): createBuildCommands() calls isCudaEnabled(), which is `#if os(Linux) ... #else return false #endif`, so on macOS it prints \"CUDA is disabled\" and returns an EMPTY command list. It emits no build commands, compiles nothing, and never invokes encuda on this platform. The companion tree Source/Encuda (the executable it would drive on Linux) is hashed too."
    },
